== B1 (round-1 BLOCKING): FIXED
Both instances of the class are fixed. writes.ts:271 (step 2, symbolic-ref)
and :286 (step 4, show-ref) now return gitFailureRefusal when
`broken || (code !== 0 && code !== 1)`. Re-enumerated every runGit call
site in writes.ts (4 total): ls-files (step 1, allows on any non-zero,
which is the brief's design), symbolic-ref (fixed), show-ref (fixed),
rev-parse in describeDetached (message text only). No other instance.
Round-1 repro rerun against the round-2 source (real repo, record
tracked, opus/W-9 exists, HEAD=master, `pack-refs --all`, then one
garbage line appended to .git/packed-refs):
  ls-files --error-unmatch opera/W-9.md    -> exit 0 (step 1 passes)
  symbolic-ref -q HEAD                     -> exit 128
  show-ref --verify --quiet refs/heads/opus/W-9 -> exit 128
  recordOwnerRefusal(<repo>/studio, W-9)   -> REFUSE "could not determine
      whether this checkout owns opus/W-9's record (D-021) — git failed;
      refusing ..."   (round 1: ALLOW)
  packed-refs restored, same call          -> REFUSE (ownership message)
Note on the repro: with no packed-refs file, a lone garbage line
yields a packed-refs that git accepts (all exits 0), so the repro needs
`pack-refs` first. The builder's test does this.
Step 1's allow-on-error is untouched: an untracked record with corrupt
packed-refs -> ls-files exit 1 -> ALLOW. A studio outside any repo ->
ALLOW.

