== Advisories (non-blocking)
R2-A1 Step 4's B1 hunk (writes.ts:286) has no test that bites. If I
  revert that hunk alone (mutate.sh revert-b1-step4), behaviours 23-30
  have 0 FAIL. Corrupting packed-refs trips step 2 first. A broken loose
  ref makes show-ref exit 1 (git's own "not found"), not 128. So in
  practice no fixture reaches step 4's failure branch on its own. Verified
  by reading instead: it is symmetric with step 2. Also, the new b1
  assertion checks "D-021", which both refusal messages carry, rather than
  the git-failure wording. A regression that refused for the wrong reason
  would still pass. Worth pinning if this path is touched again.
R2-A2 (carried, accepted) A4: `ci --opus` from the trunk still runs every
  CI step before verify refuses. Unchanged, and outside the brief.

